      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] ✅ **LGTM with minor suggestions** — See inline comments for optional improvements. [[trajectory](go/traj/0da73ffc-ae20-4abe-8f15-02674ebf73d7)]\n\n### Review Summary\n\n*   **Functionality:** The approach of acquiring the mapped storage lock before disabling the MPU protection effectively resolves the mutex contention issue while the MPU is disabled.\n*   **Style \u0026 Consistency:** I have left inline comments recommending `#ifdef CONFIG_EXTERNAL_STORAGE` instead of `IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_PLATFORM_EC_EXTERNAL_STORAGE)` in `common/rollback.c` to maintain consistency with the rest of the file and ensure compatibility with legacy EC builds.\n*   **Security:** This patch improves the security posture by minimizing the window where MPU hardware protection is disabled, ensuring that any waiting on mutexes happens while protection is active.\n*   **Testing \u0026 Coverage:** Excellent job adding a dedicated hardware test (`rollback_lock.c`) to explicitly verify the lock/unlock ordering and intercepting the function to validate the behavior. The test correctly handles both external and internal storage platforms. \n*   **CL Size \u0026 Scope:** The CL is appropriately scoped to this specific bug fix and is easy to reason about.\n\nTAG\u003dagy\nCONV\u003d9c42ef96-fd17-4138-bb44-418eb7eb260e",
