      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] This should use `#ifdef CONFIG_EXTERNAL_STORAGE` instead of `IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_PLATFORM_EC_EXTERNAL_STORAGE)`.\n\n`common/rollback.c` is compiled for both Zephyr and legacy EC builds. In legacy EC builds, Zephyr-specific Kconfig prefixes like `CONFIG_PLATFORM_EC_` do not exist, so `IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_PLATFORM_EC_EXTERNAL_STORAGE)` will unconditionally evaluate to false. \n\nUsing `#ifdef CONFIG_EXTERNAL_STORAGE` is compatible with both build systems (Zephyr\u0027s EC shim maps the Zephyr config to `CONFIG_EXTERNAL_STORAGE` in `config_zephyr.h`, and legacy EC uses it natively), and matches the existing `#ifdef` usage in `zephyr/shim/src/flash.c`.",
